  "title": "Gabriela Mistral",
  "summary": "Born Lucila Godoy Alcayaga in Vicuña, Coquimbo, Chile, she began teaching at 15 and took the pen name Gabriela Mistral. Her first major book, Desolación, appeared in 1922. She became the first Latin American author to win the Nobel Prize in literature, in 1945, and died in 1957 in New York state.",
